# ---------------------------------------------------------------- PEN-10: general part keeps the id; Mor's joining clause to PEN-45
OLD10 = """### PEN-10 General pension fund
- Rule: A general pension fund (קרן פנסיה כללית) is defined in the extension order as a new pension fund that is not entitled to designated bonds. A member of the comprehensive fund whose deposits exceed the comprehensive ceiling is joined to the same manager's general fund automatically, even without a joining request, from the date the excess deposit is received. The excess is transferred by the fifth day of the month after the deposit, and no management fee is charged on the transfer itself.
- Conditions / exceptions: The management fee on money transferred from the comprehensive fund may not exceed the member's comprehensive-fund fee rate, unless agreed otherwise with the member, employer or employee organisation (comprehensive bylaws section 18(ב)-(ג)). The manager notifies the member in writing within 14 days of the first transfer, including the lack or existence of insurance cover on that part of the salary and the option to buy cover. The general fund is not an eligible fund for the guaranteed-return mechanism (PEN-18 lists only old and new comprehensive funds).
- Figures: fee caps 4% of deposits and 1.05% a year of balance (PEN-21). Insured-salary cap 4x average wage.
- Source: [צו הרחבה (נוסח משולב) לפנסיה חובה, ילקוט הפרסומים 6302, 27.9.2011](https://www.gov.il/BlobFolder/guide/labor-wage/he/workers-rights_working-conditions_pension_H096.pdf) p.2, s.2 definitions · checked 2026-10-25 · primary; [Mor general bylaws 01.04.2026](https://www.moreinvest.co.il/media/hphjzxvl/תקנון-קרן-פנסיה-כללית.pdf), sections 8, 14, 18 · checked 2026-10-25 · institution; [Mor comprehensive bylaws 01.06.2025](https://www.moreinvest.co.il/media/ckfdk24k/תקנון-קרן-פנסיה-מקיפה-6-2025.pdf), section 18 · checked 2026-10-25 · institution.
- Dimensions: deposit-ceiling, fee-management-balance, fee-deposit, insurance-cover
- Likely to change: no
"""
NEW10 = """### PEN-10 General pension fund
- Rule: A general pension fund (קרן פנסיה כללית) is "קופת גמל לקצבה שאינה קופת ביטוח, שאושרה לראשונה אחרי יום כ"ט בטבת התשנ"ה (1 בינואר 1995) ושנקבע לגביה כי אינה זכאית לרכוש איגרת חוב מיועדת" (Income Tax Rules (Approval and Management of Provident Funds), 1964, reg. 1, "קרן חדשה כללית"). Deposits for a comprehensive-fund member above the comprehensive fund's monthly deposit ceiling (or above the partial-disability deposit ceiling, or for a fully disabled member) "יועברו לחשבון על שם העמית בקרן הכללית עד ליום החמישי בחודש העוקב לחודש שבו בוצעה ההפקדה"; they go straight to the general fund, and no management fee is charged on them in the comprehensive fund (CMA standard pension bylaw, s.18(א)).
- Conditions / exceptions: The balance fee on that money may not exceed the member's balance fee in the comprehensive fund, and the deposit fee may not exceed the lower of the comprehensive fund's deposit fee and the general fund's maximum, unless expressly agreed otherwise with the member, the employer or an employee organisation (s.18(ב)-(ג)). The manager tells the member in writing, within 14 days of the first transfer, of the transfer, the fees, whether that part of the salary carries insurance cover and, if not, the option to buy it (s.18(ד)). Every comprehensive fund writes its bylaws on the standard text (circular 2016-3-4, s.2(א)). The general fund is not an eligible fund for the guaranteed-return mechanism (PEN-18 lists only old and new comprehensive funds). Corrected 2026-10-26 (scope settling): the definition is the 1964 rules', not the extension order's (the order has no such definition), and the transfer terms are the CMA standard bylaw's; the Mor bylaws are no longer cited. Mor's wording that a member is joined to the general fund even without a joining request, from the date the excess deposit arrives, moved to PEN-45 on 2026-10-26.
- Figures: transfer by the 5th of the next month; notice within 14 days. Fee caps 4% of deposits and 1.05% a year of balance (PEN-21). A general fund's determining-salary cap is in each fund's own bylaws (Mor's: PEN-38).
- Source: """ + RULES64 + """, p.4, reg. 1 "קרן חדשה כללית" "ושנקבע לגביה כי אינה זכאית לרכוש איגרת חוב מיועדת" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary; """ + PRISHA + """, p.18, s.18(א)-(ד) "יועברו לחשבון על שם העמית בקרן הכללית עד ליום החמישי בחודש העוקב לחודש שבו בוצעה ההפקדה" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (third-party host); """ + CIRC + """
- Dimensions: deposit-ceiling, fee-management-balance, fee-deposit, insurance-cover
- Likely to change: no

### PEN-45 Mor: a member is joined to the general fund without a joining request
- Rule: Mor's general pension fund bylaws say that a comprehensive-fund member whose deposits exceed the comprehensive fund's monthly deposit ceiling (or a disabled member whose deposits exceed the ceiling permitted for a disabled member) "יצורף לקרן הכללית אף אם לא התקבלה בקרן בקשת הצטרפות בשלו", and that the joining date is the date the deposit above the ceiling was received (s.14(א)-(ב)).
- Conditions / exceptions: Split from PEN-10 on 2026-10-26 (scope settling). The general rule is the CMA standard pension bylaw s.18(א), which sends the excess to an account in the member's name in the general fund (PEN-10). The CMA's general-fund circular 2017-3-2 ("הוראות לניהול קרן חדשה כללית", prisha.co.il copy) has no joining clause (searched "בקשת הצטרפות", "יצורף", "תקרת ההפקדה": not found, 2026-10-26); other managers' general-fund bylaws were not read.
- Figures: none.
- Source: """ + MORGEN + """, p.16, s.14(א)-(ב) "יצורף לקרן הכללית אף אם לא התקבלה בקרן בקשת הצטרפות בשלו" · checked 2026-10-26 · institution. The general rule: PEN-10.
- Scope: institution: Mor
- Dimensions: eligibility, deposit-ceiling
- Likely to change: no
"""
rep(OLD10, NEW10)

